{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space","id":1041573,"title":"Slicing a Person in Half via Space","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T16:55:23-08:00","id":1041573,"title":"Slicing a Person in Half via Space","content":"Setting this thread up to continue the discussion made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban/page4\">here</a>, regarding this query:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039873#post1039873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: What Practice would you place slicing someone in half via Space at?<br /> Not a direct damage spell - one that functions as a Portal Slice.</div> </div> </div> </div> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041233#post1041233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Are you saying that you need to be a master to cut a tree for a fireplace?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of using the Space Arcanum alone, I would say yes, you would need to apply unmaking if you were not inflicting damage to the tree in order to cause that tree to sever. The original nature of the query was what practice it would take to slice a person apart, without it being a damaging spell. By nature of warping around a person's limbs - or pulling upon a person's limbs - you are, effectively, inflicting damage in order to sever the arm - hardly much different than if you took a sword and cut a person. In order to actually disconnect a part of a person from another part of their body - fully and completely - one would need to remove the connection that exists there in the first place.<br /> <br /> This is assuming that the limb in question is not still connected. A person whose arm is sent through a portal is still technically connected to their arm, even if to our eyes it seems like it is severed, and even if due to the illusion of distance a person is incapable of using it properly for their immediate enviroment. At this point, however, this 'severance' is an illusion - the arm is not really cut off, it is just distanced from one part of iy. When the spell expired, when the magic is gone - the arms would still be attached to the other person, because it is still connected. <br /> <br /> Creating a portal slice would essentially require removing that same connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041247#post1041247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I am understanding from this is:<br /> <br /> To cause the sympathy of something with itself (not just something an intimate connection, but actually part of the same thing) to be severed so severely that it isn't even part of the same thing anymore is to <i>unmake that sympathy in a fell swoop</i>, thus the unmake practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my thought process, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:30:42-08:00","id":1041696,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the discussion I took a crack at creating such a spell.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Clean Cut</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaponry, Craft, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage destroys the connection between the subject and a part of itself of a Size equal to the Potency of the spell, separating them irrevocably. Using this effect on living beings can be instantly fatal when severing their heads or spines. Severing limbs and other extremities it\u2019s not instantly fatal, but deals the spell Potency in lethal damage and applies the Bleeding tilt, in addition of severing the extremity. The effects of this spell are Lasting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Life </span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The spell doesn\u2019t cause any damage or bleeding, leaving a cauterized stump.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:49:12-08:00","id":1041699,"title":"","content":"A question here that I couldn't make because I couldn't join in on that previous discussion in time:<br /> <br /> By the time you have Space 5, you can obliterate someone by erasing the space they're standing in. Why go for the weaker option?<br /> <br /> On Body Slice itself, I feel like it could be also done with a variation of Collapse (Space 4) that wedges in empty air instead of nearby objects, or by making a portal designed to close violently (Space 3 since that's where we get Co-Location), or by even Making empty space between a limb and its stump (Space 5 again).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:22:39-08:00","id":1041712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041699#post1041699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the time you have Space 5, you can obliterate someone by erasing the space they're standing in. Why go for the weaker option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, you just want to send a message.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041696#post1041696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by the discussion I took a crack at creating such a spell.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Clean Cut</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaponry, Craft, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage destroys the connection between the subject and a part of itself of a Size equal to the Potency of the spell, separating them irrevocably. Using this effect on living beings can be instantly fatal when severing their heads or spines. Severing limbs and other extremities it\u2019s not instantly fatal, but deals the spell Potency in lethal damage and applies the Bleeding tilt, in addition of severing the extremity. The effects of this spell are Lasting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Life </span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The spell doesn\u2019t cause any damage or bleeding, leaving a cauterized stump.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Forces should have an addon for cauterization as well. <br /> Also, although the spells in the book follow the pattern, there's no actual requirement of matching dot levels for conjunctional effects. This would probably be Life 4, although Forces 5 would still be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 02-01-2017, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:24:35-08:00","id":1041714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041696#post1041696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by the discussion I took a crack at creating such a spell.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Clean Cut</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaponry, Craft, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage destroys the connection between the subject and a part of itself of a Size equal to the Potency of the spell, separating them irrevocably. Using this effect on living beings can be instantly fatal when severing their heads or spines. Severing limbs and other extremities it\u2019s not instantly fatal, but deals the spell Potency in lethal damage and applies the Bleeding tilt, in addition of severing the extremity. The effects of this spell are Lasting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Life </span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The spell doesn\u2019t cause any damage or bleeding, leaving a cauterized stump.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't severed limbs be aggravated damage? Still, awesome spell there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:25:15-08:00","id":1041715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041712#post1041712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, you just want to send a message.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T02:57:15-08:00","id":1041751,"title":"","content":"It's a continuation of a thread mentioned in the opening post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041512#post1041512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a neat artifact. I don't view this so much as a problem, but rather as an enjoyable debate. While I'd like to be right (and ultimately will be even if I am not current, since I am willing to change my point of view if given evidence to do so), I am also just having fun chatting about arcane minutiae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I also like to talk about how things work when it comes to arcana. If I didn't I wouldn't be here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that the Arcanum cares neither for life nor death. It seemed you were referencing Space as a location within the three axis of absolute dimensional measurement, rather than a gross relative confluence of connections between <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/thing\" target=\"_blank\">things</a>, in that last sentence. Is that your stance for the Arcanum? My interpretation is the latter. By the way, I am really enjoying your ability to articulate your point of view and reference material to back up your assertions. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I think that Space is both dimensions and connections and you don't need to go the hard way to achieve desired effect. Look at Heightened Senses form Life, it could easly be a Perfecting spell. Before errata it was Rulling which is fine too, but now its Unveiling(it should be Compelling IMO). So while cutting limbs with Fraying is impossible doing it with Unmaking is an overkill and show off which leaves us with Unraveling. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:32:50-08:00","id":1041822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041712#post1041712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, you just want to send a message.<br /> <br /> <br /> Forces should have an addon for cauterization as well.<br /> Also, although the spells in the book follow the pattern, there's no actual requirement of matching dot levels for conjunctional effects. This would probably be Life 4, although Forces 5 would still be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is Life 4, but I was thinking that maybe 3 and a Reach is enough? But as someone suggested, maybe the damage should be aggravated, and then it should definetily be Life 4 and maybe a reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:46:22-08:00","id":1041826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041699#post1041699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question here that I couldn't make because I couldn't join in on that previous discussion in time:<br /> <br /> By the time you have Space 5, you can obliterate someone by erasing the space they're standing in. Why go for the weaker option?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your intent is to kill, you can go for that but a spell like the one I posted would also be useful at splitting inanimate objects and butchering corpses or soon to be corpses instantly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:46:38-08:00","id":1041827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041822#post1041822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is Life 4, but I was thinking that maybe 3 and a Reach is enough? But as someone suggested, maybe the damage should be aggravated, and then it should definetily be Life 4 and maybe a reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently I suck at counting dots.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind if you make it aggravated damage, using it will always cost a point of Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:23:04-08:00","id":1041839,"title":"","content":"At Arcanum 3 you may deal bashing damage and tilt, or a non-persistant condition.<br /> <br /> At Arcanum 4 you can allly a persistant tilt.<br /> <br /> At 5 you can do whatever you want.<br /> <br /> So at 3 you fray the connection between the likb and the body. The bond still exists, but is weakened. Their arm falls off, but it is still functionally attached. They can move it and blood still flows normally.<br /> <br /> At 4 you can change the soace entirely, severing the limb. Severing the head or vital organs doesnt work because the head / vital organs *is* the self.<br /> <br /> At 5 you can turn the person into goo by seperatjng all their cells if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:40:40-08:00","id":1041845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041839#post1041839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At 4 you can change the soace entirely, severing the limb. Severing the head or vital organs doesnt work because the head / vital organs *is* the self.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to understand your view and it would help if I knew whether this was a reflection of your understanding of the Practices in general, or Space specifically - would you allow Life 4 to transform someone into a lungless human, or would you require Life 5 for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:46:21-08:00","id":1041850,"title":"","content":"The 4th dot may create persistant conditions. You need 5 dots toncomoletely dismantle someone with a spell without it being via damage. Theres even a sidebar on transforming people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:51:28-08:00","id":1041854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041850#post1041850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 4th dot may create persistant conditions. You need 5 dots toncomoletely dismantle someone with a spell without it being via damage. Theres even a sidebar on transforming people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And would you consider transforming someone into a lungless human (that is doomed to suffocate and die) simple 'transformation' or 'dismantling someone with a spell'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:55:24-08:00","id":1041856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041850#post1041850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 4th dot may create persistant conditions. You need 5 dots toncomoletely dismantle someone with a spell without it being via damage. Theres even a sidebar on transforming people.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Life 4 you can transform someone so it doesn't have an arm, but because the shape traits of living organisms is what Life is about. To me, there's no different between the head or the heart and a pinky, so that's why you need Space 5 to completely sever any part of a &quot;thing&quot; from itself (whithout any kind of force or trauma, that would be different as it was established).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:05:26-08:00","id":1041860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041854#post1041854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And would you consider transforming someone into a lungless human (that is doomed to suffocate and die) simple 'transformation' or 'dismantling someone with a spell'?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, assuming it was a death sentance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:13:32-08:00","id":1041866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041860#post1041860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter, assuming it was a death sentance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting take. I disagree strongly, although I am leaning towards considering a Portal Slice style effect to be Unmaking anyway, for different reasons.<br /> <br /> Shoving all effects that can kill someone without causing damage into the Practice of Unmaking isn't consistent, honestly. You can turn all of the air around them solid with State Change and they'll suffocate all the same, or you can kill someone with Psychic Domination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:34:36-08:00","id":1041871,"title":"","content":"I'm actually inclined to agree with Inodiv on the lungless human effect honestly - yes, you need air to survive, but unlike with a portal slice split through center mass it's not going to automatically kill you (rather, its more likely to inflict suffocation damage over time.) Using life to create someone without proper set of lungs would be life 4 - and, if the person did not find a way to breath before the duration expired, and if the duration lasted longer than the person could go without air, then that would very much kill them. That said, transforming a person into a lungless human is much different from removing their lungs entirely and leaving a bloody, gaping hole inside of them. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a> I like your spell. I recommend that instead inflicting one lethal per potency when the person is choosing to sever limbs instead of just kill their target, that you fill their entire health track with lethal and then inflict one more lethal per potency (effectively filling them full of lethal, then rolling over, while bleeding out). My reasoning for this is because severing someone's arm is not what I would envision to be 1 lethal, and even things which can regenerate should take longer than a turn to recover from that. Adding the life effect might remove the damage entirely (so that there is nothing to heal), or it could simply make it so that they are stabilized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":".  Typo 02-01-2017, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:14:16-08:00","id":1041895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041871#post1041871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">inflicting one lethal per success</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what the spell does, and not how spells work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:24:23-08:00","id":1041902,"title":"","content":"Any and all efforts spent trying to justify why one of Mage's few limitations don't apply could and probably instead should be spent making them appear thematically consistent and awesome within those limits.<br /> <br /> It is true that almost all Arcana, by the third dot, have a way to reliably end the life of someone. Almost all of those ways are more interesting or involved than &quot;zap you dead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-05-2017, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:06:10-08:00","id":1041926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041902#post1041902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true that almost all Arcana, by the third dot, have a way to reliably end the life of someone. Almost all of those ways are more interesting or involved than &quot;zap you dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:11:25-08:00","id":1041950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041871#post1041871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a> I like your spell. I recommend that instead inflicting one lethal per success when the person is choosing to sever limbs instead of just kill their target, that you fill their entire health track with lethal and then inflict one more lethal per potency (effectively filling them full of lethal, then rolling over, while bleeding out). My reasoning for this is because severing someone's arm is not what I would envision to be 1 lethal, and even things which can regenerate should take longer than a turn to recover from that. Adding the life effect might remove the damage entirely (so that there is nothing to heal), or it could simply make it so that they are stabilized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say an arm is around Size 3, so the spell's Potency would have to be 3. With 3 lethal levels AND THE BLEEDING TILT most people would lose conciousness in 4 turns and die in 11. That's around half a minute. We've been considering making the damage aggravated, but honestly I think that would be overkill. Afterall, people DO survive amputations when they are treated. And they even did before painkillers and penicilin and modern medical procedures. So I think it's the right balance between being incredibly dangerous but giving and actual chance of survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:45:24-08:00","id":1041965,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041895#post1041895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not what the spell does, and not how spells work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was a typo. Fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041950#post1041950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say an arm is around Size 3, so the spell's Potency would have to be 3. With 3 lethal levels AND THE BLEEDING TILT most people would lose conciousness in 4 turns and die in 11. That's around half a minute. We've been considering making the damage aggravated, but honestly I think that would be overkill. Afterall, people DO survive amputations when they are treated. And they even did before painkillers and penicilin and modern medical procedures. So I think it's the right balance between being incredibly dangerous but giving and actual chance of survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>*considers* I did, actually miss that the potency needs to exceed the size of the target. That brings a whole different matter. In my view, I would say that the withstand should be the only thing that actually needs to be accounted for - and that so long as you surpassed that withstand, you ideally should be capable of cutting off whatever you want to cut off. If you want them killed/dead/done, lop off their head or split them through the middle and call it a day. If you want them removed of their arm, then they lose their arm (or leg, or fingers). (Now... if the withstand is size and not their stamina, that's another matter)<br /> <br /> Now I'm all for noting varying degrees of damage severity depending on what you cut off. Slicing a person's arm clean off is not going to have the same effect that slicing their finger will.<br /> <br /> That said - it does not take 6 days recover from losing an arm - immediately tended to or not - before your back up and able to function properly (naturally, I'm speaking sans limb - unless your a werewolf or vampire, in which case your limb did regenerate and likely within the same scene). I know the damage systems are a bit abstract, but at the very least recovering from this kind of injury should be difficult at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:55:45-08:00","id":1041972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space?p=1041950#post1041950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say an arm is around Size 3, so the spell's Potency would have to be 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale handles size, not Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:18:16-08:00","id":1041993,"title":"","content":"I can't really tell where we are with Unraveling/ Unmaking dilemma so I just leave this here.<br /> Unraveling kills people reliably by RAW.<br /> 3 Gnosis + 4 Arcanum + 3 Yantra + 3 WP - 8 for Potency = 5<br /> 5 dice for a potency 7 spell which deals aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 02-01-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:32:31-08:00","id":1042225,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>: Scale handles the size of the target, the spell is not targeting the arm but the person. Spells like Shrink and Grow use Potency to alter Size so I don't see it as a problem. It was the best way I could find to avoid doing massive damage for removing a pinky or a nail or doing almost no damage for removivng a massive chunk of the body.<br /> <br /> @Jakondite: I don't see any problem with needing to reach a Potency minimum after Withstand to get the specific outcome you want. This happens with many spells. As for the recovery time, I don't know, I think if you don't bleed out and don't die from an infection, then it shouldn't be so hard to recover from an amputation. Again, people do it relatively often. I'll say that maybe the Bleeding tilt is not grave enough for the massive hemorrage this would cause. You could replace it for a Massive Hemorrage tilt that does lethal instead of bashing and requires a hard Medicine roll to remove (something like Dexterity+Medicine-patient's current damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T12:04:34-08:00","id":1045895,"title":"","content":"Cutting a person in half with Space is probably Unraveling and Withstood. <br /> <br /> Since I handle Withstand a little differently, in my game you would inflict lethal Potency damage and if that exceeds Withstand, you sever a whole body part off. <br /> <br /> In the other topic, you can completely disable someone with a straightforward Adept spell (and do so indirectly with even simpler spells, depending on your specific situation). Master spells are more about showing off than doing anything practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}